invariant: INV-13
file: tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh tcp_nonblocking_in
reason: ch_record_in reads the peer's bytes while a record it staged is
  still uncollected, so a step can stage a second record over the first
  one in t.tx. The tcp_nonblocking_in proof asserts that a staged record
  refuses input with CH_EINVAL, and fails on this edit.

--- old
    if (r->tx_len != 0) {
        return CH_EINVAL;
    }
    size_t off = 0;
--- new
    size_t off = 0;
